Z||000023||artherd||12-26-2001||12:57 AM||||IIICK!!!!<P>I like the Jalapeno, but that 'lambo' wannabe creation from hell in the corner has got to take the cake.<P>We really ought to stop this thread, it pops up every now and then, and all that happens is a lot of bitching, and then some forum member's car gets mentioned, and we all leave with a bad taste in our mouths.<P>Merry Christmas.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Smoooooth GT:<BR><B>I'm sorry for this because I know some of you actually like this.. YUKKO!!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Disappointed_anim_1.gif">  <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Jalapeno_Body_Kit.jpg">  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000024||jelly2m8||12-26-2001||01:08 AM|||| I had a parts Fiero that beat all those for uglyness. Too bad I naver took any pics before i scrapped it.<P> Imagine this,<P>Black 85 GT, paint seriusly faded, red ground effects. whaletail spoiler that was about half the size it should have been.<P> Had the uglest pinstrip job, was probably red pinstripe, looked pink when i got it. Started at leading edge of fenders, got wider as it went back and turned into a bow or somekind of a swirl on the doors. same pinstrip effect on the decklid.<P> After market sunroof, gaudy hood vents that were crooked.<P> The wheels were painted red. I still have those kicking around, should snap some pics.<P> It had chicken wire mesh in place of the lower airdam under the nose.<P> 2 cell phone antennas, one on the windshield, the other on the back window. Still had one of those real old car phones that was permanitely attached to the car. The hand set was mounted to the top of the radio surround.<P> Dunno what the guy was thinking, it was probably a nice car before he went physco with it.<P> It was sooo ugly, that even sitting out back my shop, I had to pull the pinstrip off of it, gave it a bit of decency in its last days....<P> Suprisingly we did salvage the ground effects,bumpers, and the motor to put on our 85 coupe. I must have used 150 bux worth of sanding discs to get that red paint off of the GFX and bumpers!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://users.eastlink.ca/~acook1/pegged%2001.jpg"> ||||reg||1
